@startuml operation-guardrails
!include state-machine-style.iuml
title Slop Machine | Guarded command delivery and recovery
caption Shared by task mutations, agent assignments, checks, handoffs and publication.

state "Command proposed\nJSON envelope + typed payload\nOperation ID + exact input references" as Proposed
state "Validate command\nSchema, producer, run ownership,\npreconditions, deadline and budget" as Validate
state "Evaluate applicable policies\nVersioned modular policies\nNeMo preferred integration" as Policy
state Decision <<choice>>
state "Record accepted operation\nDurable outbox / journal intent" as Accepted
state "Claim dispatch + recheck\nOwnership, freshness and policy binding" as Dispatch
state "Execute bounded action\nStream messages, tools and usage" as Execute
state "Verify and record result\nCorrelation, snapshot, side effects\nFreshness before state transition" as Verify
state "Completed\nReturn typed result to caller" as Completed <<success>>
state "Reconcile outcome\nInspect existing side effects\nStop/fence abandoned executor" as Reconcile <<attention>>
state "Backoff / wait for readiness\nRate limit, auth or provider recovery\nBounded deadline and attempt count" as Backoff
state "Rejected / attention\nNo implicit permission on failure" as Rejected <<attention>>
state "Scope blocker\nOnly bounded handoff may proceed" as ScopeBlock <<blocked>>
state "Stop / cancel operation\nRecord partial or unknown effects" as Stop
state "Cancelled\nLate results retained as evidence only" as Cancelled <<attention>>

[*] --> Proposed
Proposed --> Validate
Validate --> Policy : structurally and contextually valid
Validate --> Rejected : malformed, stale, unauthorized,\nexpired, or budget exhausted
Policy --> Decision : evaluation completed
Decision --> Accepted : [allow]
Decision --> ScopeBlock : [confirmed necessary out-of-scope work]
Decision --> Rejected : [other block or clarification required]
Policy --> Backoff : evaluation unavailable; retry permitted\n/ do not execute
Accepted --> Dispatch
Dispatch --> Execute : no prior completion; execution claim current
Dispatch --> Verify : existing result / deduplicate delivery
Dispatch --> Reconcile : prior attempt outcome unknown
Dispatch --> Rejected : preconditions no longer valid
Execute --> Verify : response or completion observed
Execute --> Reconcile : timeout, crash, or ambiguous external effect
Verify --> Completed : valid completed domain result recorded
Verify --> Backoff : confirmed retryable failure;\nno ambiguous effects; retry budget remains
Verify --> Rejected : confirmed non-retryable operation failure
Verify --> Reconcile : outcome cannot be confirmed
Verify --> Rejected : stale or conflicting terminal result
Reconcile --> Verify : completed effect found
Reconcile --> Backoff : safe to retry; executor stopped/fenced;\nretry budget remains
Reconcile --> Rejected : unsafe retry or exhausted recovery
Backoff --> Validate : readiness restored / revalidate same operation
Backoff --> Rejected : deadline/recovery budget exceeded
Execute --> Stop : cancellation or hard limit
Backoff --> Stop : cancellation
Dispatch --> Stop : cancellation before execution
Stop --> Cancelled : executor stopped/fenced; effects recorded
Completed --> [*]
Rejected --> [*]
ScopeBlock --> [*]
Cancelled --> [*]

note right of Verify
  Execution completed is not domain approval:
  a completed review may request changes;
  a completed test may fail.
  The calling task state decides the next stage.
end note
note left of Dispatch
  Stable operation/message IDs across redelivery.
  A new repair assignment gets a NEW operation ID.
  At-least-once delivery; reconcile external effects.
  A record of acceptance is not proof of completion.
end note
note bottom of Execute
  Only intercepted tool calls can be blocked before execution.
  Record observed-only / unavailable enforcement explicitly.
  Every event carries task/run/session/operation correlation where applicable.
  Deterministic permissions remain enforced outside model judgment.
  Agent plans, results and role handoffs use output-handoff-policy.puml;
  this command gate alone does not contain output drift.
end note
@enduml
